From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 21:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] luma: the Shell wears the glass veil applications wear

In Frost and Glass the Shelf islands, Quick Options, the calendar and the
dock were one veil (80%/62%) and Shell popup menus, dock labels, previews and
folders another (88%/80%), and neither was the veil application windows use
for their title band, context menus and popovers (90%/85%). Quick Options and
an application context menu, open side by side, were visibly two materials.

luma-shelf.css now states the veil once, for every one of those surfaces:
Frost rgba(248,249,250,0.90) and Glass rgba(250,250,251,0.85), the values in
config/shared/design-tokens.json. The rules that used to paint each surface
keep their border, ink and shadow and no longer set a fill, so there is one
place to change it. Text on the veil carries no shadow. The ink ledger in
lumaSurfaceMaterials.js carries the same values, so its contrast gate
measures what is painted.
---
 data/theme/gnome-shell-light.css |  4 +-
 data/theme/luma-shelf.css        | 74 ++++++++++++++++----------------
 js/ui/lumaSurfaceMaterials.js    |  9 ++--
 3 files changed, 46 insertions(+), 41 deletions(-)

