+/* The glass veil: the one definition. In Frost and Glass every Shell surface
+ * that stands or floats over the desktop -- the Shelf islands (the dock, the
+ * clock, live chips), Quick Options, the clock's calendar, every Shell popup
+ * menu, and the dock's labels, previews and folders -- is painted with the
+ * veil application windows use for their title band, context menus and
+ * popovers (config/shared/design-tokens.json, surface_treatments.*.surface_veil),
+ * so Quick Options and an application's context menu are one material. No
+ * other rule paints these surfaces in Frost or Glass: the rules above only
+ * carry border, ink and shadow. ProjectLuma's tools/check-shell-veil.py fails
+ * the build if another rule does, or if these values drift from the tokens.
+ * Text on the veil is plain; the veil carries its own contrast. */
+.luma-shelf-material.luma-surface-frost,
+.luma-shelf-root.luma-shelf-separate > .luma-shelf-group >
+.luma-shelf-actions-island >
+.luma-shelf-material.luma-status-cluster.luma-surface-frost,
+.popup-menu.luma-surface-frost .popup-menu-content,
